---Garnishments, or employee deductions, are fixed amounts or percentages deducted from an employee’s pay. They can be deducted a specific number of times or on a recurring basis. Garnishments can also have maximum deductions on a yearly or per-pay-period bases. Common uses for garnishments are court-ordered payments for child support or back taxes. Some companies provide loans to their employees that are repaid via garnishments.
---@class gusto.Garnishment
---@field active? boolean Whether or not this garnishment is currently active.
---@field amount? string The amount of the garnishment. Either a percentage or a fixed dollar amount. Represented as a float, e.g. "8.00".
---@field annual_maximum? string|distilled.Null The maximum deduction per annum. A null value indicates no maximum. Represented as a float, e.g. "200.00".
---@field child_support? gusto.GarnishmentChildSupport|distilled.Null
---@field court_ordered? boolean Whether the garnishment is court ordered.
---@field deduct_as_percentage? boolean Whether the amount should be treated as a percentage to be deducted per pay period.
---@field description? string The description of the garnishment.
---@field employee_uuid? string The UUID of the employee to which this garnishment belongs.
---@field garnishment_type? gusto.GarnishmentGarnishmentType|distilled.Null The specific type of garnishment for court ordered garnishments.
---@field pay_period_maximum? string|distilled.Null The maximum deduction per pay period. A null value indicates no maximum. Represented as a float, e.g. "16.00".
---@field recurring? boolean Whether the garnishment should recur indefinitely.
---@field times? number|distilled.Null The number of times to apply the garnishment. Ignored if recurring is true.
---@field total_amount? string|distilled.Null A maximum total deduction for the lifetime of this garnishment. A null value indicates no maximum.
---@field uuid string The UUID of the garnishment in Gusto.
---@field version? string The current version of the object. See the [versioning guide](https://docs.gusto.com/embedded-payroll/docs/idempotency) for information on how to use this field.

