---@field coverage_salary_multiplier? string|distilled.Null The coverage amount as a multiple of the employee's salary. Only applicable for Group Term Life benefits. Note: cannot be set if coverage amount is also set.
---@field deduct_as_percentage? boolean Whether the employee deduction amount should be treated as a percentage to be deducted from each payroll.
---@field deduction_reduces_taxable_income? gusto.GetEmployeeBenefitResponseDeductionReducesTaxableIncome|distilled.Null Whether the employee deduction reduces taxable income or not. Only valid for Group Term Life benefits. Note: when the value is not "unset", coverage amount and coverage salary multiplier are ignored.
---@field effective_date? string The date the employee benefit will start.
---@field elective? boolean Whether the company contribution is elective (aka matching). For "tiered" contribution types, this is always true.
---@field employee_deduction? string The amount to be deducted, per pay period, from the employee's pay.
---@field employee_deduction_annual_maximum? string|distilled.Null The maximum employee deduction amount per year. A null value signifies no limit.
---@field expiration_date? string|distilled.Null The date the employee benefit will expire. A null value indicates the benefit will not expire.
---@field limit_option? string|distilled.Null Some benefits require additional information to determine their limit. `Family` and `Individual` are applicable to HSA benefit. `Joint Filing or Single` and `Married and Filing Separately` are applicable to Dependent Care FSA benefit.
---@field retirement_loan_identifier? string|distilled.Null Identifier for a 401(k) loan assigned by the 401(k) provider
---@field version? string The current version of the object. See the [versioning guide](https://docs.gusto.com/embedded-payroll/docs/idempotency) for information on how to use this field.
---@field company_benefit_uuid? string The UUID of the company benefit.
---@field employee_uuid? string The UUID of the employee to which the benefit belongs.
---@field uuid string The UUID of the employee benefit.

---An object representing the type and value of the company contribution.
---@class gusto.GetEmployeeBenefitResponseContribution
---@field type? string The company contribution scheme. "amount": The company contributes a fixed amount per payroll. If elective is true, the contribution is matching, dollar-for-dollar. "percentage": The company contributes a percentage of the payroll amount per payroll period. If elective is true, the contribution is matching, dollar-for-dollar. "tiered": The company contribution varies according to the size of the employee deduction.
---@field value? gusto.GetEmployeeBenefitResponseContributionValue For the `amount` and `percentage` contribution types, the value of the corresponding amount or percentage. For the `tiered` contribution type, an array of tiers.

---For the `amount` and `percentage` contribution types, the value of the corresponding amount or percentage.
---
---For the `tiered` contribution type, an array of tiers.
---@alias gusto.GetEmployeeBenefitResponseContributionValue string|gusto.GetEmployeeBenefitResponseContributionValueCase1

---@class gusto.GetEmployeeBenefitResponseContributionValueCase1
---@field tiers? gusto.GetEmployeeBenefitResponseContributionValueCase1TiersList

---A single tier of a tiered matching scheme.
---@class gusto.GetEmployeeBenefitResponseContributionValueCase1TiersItem
---@field rate? string The percentage of employee deduction within this tier the company contribution will match.
---@field threshold? string Specifies the upper limit (inclusive) percentage of the employee contribution that this tier applies to. Use threshold to define each tier's end point, with tiers applied cumulatively from 0% upwards. For example: If the first tier has a threshold of "3", and `rate` of "100", the company will match 100% of employee contributions from 0% up to and including 3% of payroll. If the next tier has a threshold of "5" and a rate of "50", the company will match 50% of contributions from above 3% up to and including 5% of payroll.
---@field threshold_delta? string The step up difference between this tier's threshold and the previous tier's threshold. In the first tier, this is equivalent to threshold.

---@alias gusto.GetEmployeeBenefitResponseContributionValueCase1TiersList gusto.GetEmployeeBenefitResponseContributionValueCase1TiersItem[]

