---@class gusto.PutEmployeeBenefitRequestContribution
---@field type? gusto.PutEmployeeBenefitRequestContributionType|string The company contribution scheme. `amount`: The company contributes a fixed amount per payroll. If elective is true, the contribution is matching, dollar-for-dollar. `percentage`: The company contributes a percentage of the payroll amount per payroll period. If elective is true, the contribution is matching, dollar-for-dollar. `tiered`: The size of the company contribution corresponds to the size of the employee deduction relative to a tiered matching scheme.
---@field value? gusto.PutEmployeeBenefitRequestContributionValue For the `amount` and `percentage` contribution types, the value of the corresponding amount or percentage. For the `tiered` contribution type, an array of tiers.

---The company contribution scheme.
---
---`amount`: The company contributes a fixed amount per payroll. If elective is true, the contribution is matching, dollar-for-dollar.
---
---`percentage`: The company contributes a percentage of the payroll amount per payroll period. If elective is true, the contribution is matching, dollar-for-dollar.
---
---`tiered`: The size of the company contribution corresponds to the size of the employee deduction relative to a tiered matching scheme.
---@alias gusto.PutEmployeeBenefitRequestContributionType "amount"|"percentage"|"tiered"

---For the `amount` and `percentage` contribution types, the value of the corresponding amount or percentage.
---
---For the `tiered` contribution type, an array of tiers.
---@alias gusto.PutEmployeeBenefitRequestContributionValue string|gusto.PutEmployeeBenefitRequestContributionValueCase1List

---A single tier of a tiered matching scheme.
---@class gusto.PutEmployeeBenefitRequestContributionValueCase1Item
---@field rate? string The percentage of employee deduction within this tier the company contribution will match.
---@field threshold? string Specifies the upper limit (inclusive) percentage of the employee contribution that this tier applies to. Use threshold to define each tier's end point, with tiers applied cumulatively from 0% upwards. For example: If the first tier has a threshold of "3", and rate of "100", the company will match 100% of employee contributions from 0% up to and including 3% of payroll. If the next tier has a threshold of "5" and a rate of "50", the company will match 50% of contributions from above 3% up to and including 5% of payroll.

---For `tiered` contribution types, an array of tiers.
---@alias gusto.PutEmployeeBenefitRequestContributionValueCase1List gusto.PutEmployeeBenefitRequestContributionValueCase1Item[]

